From f3e1d1400feb3a4f597a4ab586e76d050481c14e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tiopex <tiopxyz@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 18:10:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: enable true inline rotation on SM8550, SM8650
 and SM8750

DPU 9.0, 10.0 and 12.0 have the SSPP true inline rotator v2.0.1 (max
pre-rotation height 1088). Expose 90/270 on the VIG pipes and program
ROT90.

Require UBWC for inline rotation of both RGB and YUV. Include
XRGB2101010 which gamescope prefers for scanout.

Keep QSEED enabled for 1:1 RGB when rotating; the rotator output
feeds the scaler (SDE does the same). DRM rotation is CCW, DPU
inline rotator is CW: XOR REFLECT_X|Y on rot90. Check pre-rotated
source height, not width. Reserve rot90 pipes with test_bit.

Merged from the three per-SoC ROCKNIX patches for a combined kernel:
one shared feature mask and rotation config, one rot_v2 sblk per
QSEED revision.

Signed-off-by: tiopex <tiopxyz@gmail.com>
